1
00:02:02,012 --> 00:02:03,919
<v Girl>Good morning, what can I do for you? 


2
00:02:03,919 --> 00:02:13,600
<v Peter>Uh, yes, I am currently visiting this area, but I injured myself when I was doing sports a while ago, and I still feel painful, so I wondered whether I could go for a doctor here. 

3
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:21,716
<v Girl>Sure sir, we can take you on as a temporary patient. I'll just take down some personal details of you. May I have your name, please? 


4
00:02:21,716 --> 00:02:23,220
<v Peter>Yes, it's Peter Smith. 


5
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:27,172
<v Girl>All right, Peter. And where are you currently staying here? 


6
00:02:27,172 --> 00:02:29,635
<v Peter>At 95 Cross Street 


7
00:02:29,635 --> 00:02:31,413
<v Girl>And the county? 

8
00:02:31,413 --> 00:02:35,667
<v Peter>Walkley. That's W-a-l-k-l-e-y. 


9
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:39,245
<v Girl>OK, and can I have a contact number? 

10
00:02:39,245 --> 00:02:44,097
<v Peter>Uh, it's 4689 5324. 

11
00:02:44,097 --> 00:02:49,437
<v Girl>OK, thanks. May you just wait down there! The doctor will see you in a minute.


12
00:03:32,187 --> 00:03:35,695
<v Doctor>Now, how can I help you? It's Peter Smith, isn't it? 


13
00:03:35,695 --> 00:03:41,244
<v Peter>Yes, I had a sporting accident, and a doctor at home treated me, but I'm still getting some pain. 


14
00:03:41,244 --> 00:03:46,421
<v Peter>Hum, right. Uh, first of all, I want to ask you a few questions. 


15
00:03:46,421 --> 00:03:47,633
<v Peter>Okay. 


16
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:50,857
<v Doctor>Well, what sport were you doing when you got injured? 


17
00:03:50,857 --> 00:03:53,245
<v Peter>Playing tennis with my friends. 


18
00:03:53,245 --> 00:03:57,742
<v Doctor>Now, I see. Did you hurt your elbow or wrist? 


19
00:03:57,742 --> 00:04:01,794
<v Peter>Oh, no. I had my knee sprained, which was the original problem. 

20
00:04:01,794 --> 00:04:04,895
<v Doctor>Right, and when did this happen? 


21
00:04:04,895 --> 00:04:08,721
<v Peter>Uh, that was three weeks ago now, so it was about June 18th. 

22
00:04:08,721 --> 00:04:11,957
<v Doctor>Hum. And, you said you had medical treatment at home? 

23
00:04:11,957 --> 00:04:18,504
<v Peter>Uh, yeah. The doctor said I didn't need an X-ray or things alike, and he just told me to use an ice pack. 


24
00:04:18,504 --> 00:04:20,613
<v Doctor>Fine, anything else? 


25
00:04:20,613 --> 00:04:24,848
<v Peter>Yes, and I've been using a walking stick to help me get around. 


26
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:28,969
<v Doctor>Right, now what problems are you having during walking? 


27
00:04:28,969 --> 00:04:34,787
<v Peter>Well, actually I can walk, yet I still can't go upstairs, so I've been sleeping downstairs. 


28
00:04:34,787 --> 00:04:38,143
<v Doctor>Hum, now you said your knee still gets hurt? 


29
00:04:38,143 --> 00:04:45,976
<v Peter>Well, no. Actually, it's getting better. It's my back that's hurting, me now. It really aches at night, and I cannot sleep well. 


30
00:04:45,976 --> 00:04:48,393
<v Doctor>Hum, I have several suggestions for that. 


31
00:04:48,393 --> 00:04:49,361
<v Peter>Great. 

32
00:04:49,361 --> 00:04:53,566
<v Doctor>First you should put the stick away as that's probably the source of the problem. 


33
00:04:53,566 --> 00:04:56,113
<v Peter>Oh, really? I wish I'd know. 

34
00:04:56,113 --> 00:05:00,450
<v Doctor>After that, I can prescribe you something to relax the muscles in your back 


35
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:09,179
<v Peter>Oh, sorry to be difficult, but I've had something like that in the past, and there were many side effects, and I don't want to take it. Would you recommend anything else? 


36
00:05:09,179 --> 00:05:18,132
<v Doctor>Well, yes. We do have a leaflet showing some exercises you can do yourself at home. If you do them every day, they'll soon be effective. 


37
00:05:18,132 --> 00:05:19,264
<v Peter>Great. I'll do that.